---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { manifest } from "../data/manifest-loader";

const sha = manifest.csv_sha256;
const fetchedDate = new Date(manifest.fetched_at).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<Base
  title="Citation Guide — PURSUE://INDEX"
  description="How to cite pursueindex.com — the corpus, individual cards, and OCR transcripts. Includes BibTeX and reproducibility notes."
>
  <article class="space-y-8 max-w-3xl">
    <header class="space-y-2">
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ CITATION GUIDE
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)]">
        How to cite pursueindex
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        A short guide for researchers, journalists, and academic readers
        using pursueindex as a reference. The source documents are
        public-domain U.S. Government work; we provide the indexing layer
        (manifest, OCR transcripts, search). This page tells you how to
        point at us correctly.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ What you are actually citing
      </h2>
      <table class="w-full text-sm border border-[color:var(--color-border)]">
        <thead class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)]">
          <tr>
            <th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)]">Claim type</th>
            <th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)]">Cite</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-t border-[color:var(--color-border)]">
            <td class="py-2 px-3">Contents of a source document</td>
            <td class="py-2 px-3 text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)]">The original DOW PDF (we're a reader)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-[color:var(--color-border)]">
            <td class="py-2 px-3">A transcribed passage as it appears here</td>
            <td class="py-2 px-3 text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)]">This site, with <code>card_id</code> and page</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-t border-[color:var(--color-border)]">
            <td class="py-2 px-3">The corpus itself, or methodology</td>
            <td class="py-2 px-3 text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)]">This site, manifest snapshot</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ Citing the corpus as a whole
      </h2>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-4 font-mono text-[12px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap"><code>{`PURSUE Index. (2026). BPS AI Software.
https://pursueindex.com
(manifest CSV SHA-256: ${sha},
 snapshot: ${fetchedDate})`}</code></pre>
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        The hash pin is the load-bearing reproducibility claim — anyone
        with the same{" "}
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">csv_sha256</code>{" "}
        is looking at the same upstream CSV bytes you cited. Both fields
        appear in this site's footer on every page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ Citing a specific document or page
      </h2>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-4 font-mono text-[12px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap"><code>{`PURSUE Index card <card_id>, p. <n>.
Sourced from U.S. Department of War, Presidential Unsealing
and Reporting System for UAP Encounters (PURSUE), Release 01 (2026).
https://pursueindex.com/card/<card_id>#page-<n>`}</code></pre>
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        Worked example — citing the McHenry affidavit from
        <a href="/finds/muroc-1947" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]"> the Muroc 1947 entry</a>:
      </p>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-4 font-mono text-[12px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap"><code>{`PURSUE Index card 99c12a9c49a91750, p. 67.
Sourced from U.S. Department of War, PURSUE Release 01 (2026).
https://pursueindex.com/card/99c12a9c49a91750#page-67`}</code></pre>
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        The <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">card_id</code>{" "}
        is stable across re-fetches —{" "}
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">sha256(asset_url || title)[:16]</code>{" "}
        — so the same card resolves the same way for every reader regardless
        of when they re-run the pipeline. Page numbers are 1-indexed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ Citing the OCR transcript itself
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        If you're quoting the OCR transcript (not the original PDF text),
        make that explicit. OCR is imperfect; the transcript is a derivative work.
      </p>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-4 font-mono text-[12px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap"><code>{`PURSUE Index OCR transcript, card <card_id>, p. <n>,
OCR engine <engine> (confidence <conf>).
https://pursueindex.com/card/<card_id>#page-<n>`}</code></pre>
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">{"<engine>"}</code>{" "}
        is either <code>surya</code> or{" "}
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-amber)]">llm-anthropic</code>{" "}
        on the current corpus; both surface inline on each card page. When
        the OCR is wrong and the original PDF text is correct, cite the
        original PDF and not us.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ Citing an IMAGE-DESCRIPTIONS snippet
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        When a search snippet you quote is bracketed with
        <code class="font-mono text-xs">[[IMAGE-DESCRIPTIONS via alex-zhang42/ufo-pursue-open-atlas, mimo-v2.5]]</code>,
        the words inside that block were written by Alex Zhang's VLM
        pipeline, not our OCR. Honest provenance means citing both
        projects: ours for the retrieval surface and the page anchor,
        Alex's for the description text itself.
      </p>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-4 font-mono text-[12px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap"><code>{`PURSUE Index card <card_id>, p. <n>, image description.
Image text via Zhang, A. (2026). ufo-pursue-open-atlas (CC0).
https://huggingface.co/datasets/alex-zhang42/ufo-pursue-open-atlas
https://pursueindex.com/card/<card_id>#page-<n>`}</code></pre>
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        See <a href="/methodology#related" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">/methodology#related</a>
        for how the augmentation works and why we keep both attributions
        on every augmented snippet.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ BibTeX
      </h2>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-4 font-mono text-[11px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre"><code>{`@misc{pursueindex2026,
  title  = {PURSUE Index},
  author = {{BPS AI Software}},
  year   = {2026},
  url    = {https://pursueindex.com},
  note   = {Manifest CSV SHA-256: ${sha.slice(0, 16)}...;
            snapshot ${fetchedDate}.
            Source: U.S. Department of War PURSUE Release 01.}
}`}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3 pt-4 border-t border-[color:var(--color-border)]">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ Reproducibility
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        The manifest is hash-pinned and version-controlled. From a clean clone of
        <a href="https://github.com/BPSAI/pursue-index" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]"> github.com/BPSAI/pursue-index</a>{" "}
        any reader can rebuild the entire index. Methodology and benchmark
        numbers live at{" "}
        <a href="/methodology" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">/methodology</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        For programmatic citation lookup — pulling the same{" "}
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">card_id</code> /{" "}
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">page</code> pair
        from a search query — see the{" "}
        <a href="/api" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">API surface</a>:
        <code>/api/retrieve</code> returns the same identifiers used in the
        forms above.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        Source documents are works of the U.S. Government and in the public
        domain. The OCR transcripts derived from them carry no additional
        copyright claim from us. Index code and this site are{" "}
        <a href="https://bpsaisoftware.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">© BPS AI Software</a>,
        licensed under the{" "}
        <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">Apache License, Version 2.0</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
